+ * prefill chunk stores its index keys and closes its blocks but attends densely. A sequence's rows
+ * close every block whose last key they write, so a rejected draft's rewrite of that key clusters
+ * the block again when it is written next.
  *
  * Under tensor parallelism an index key sums every KV head and an index query every query head of
- * the layer, so each rank holds a partial projection; the all_reduce that would join them is not
- * declared yet, and a deployment above one rank is refused. */
+ * the layer. A rank whose heads are a plain split of the layer's (no replication, no attention-zero
+ * rank) writes its heads' sums to `part`, an exact f32 all_reduce joins them, and the store
+ * finishes from the sum; with one KV head a rank the sum is the one-rank sum to the bit. */
